export anchor GreenPhosphorStyle:
    number: 289
    screen: CodeRepository
    name: Green phosphor
    idea: The whole review is one glowing green-on-black terminal transcript, each part of the screen printed as the output of a command, with inverse-video highlights, ruled output boxes and a blinking block cursor waiting at the end.
    base: dark
    palette:
        black: #030803, the page and the style sheet background
        well: #0a1a0d, output boxes, the comment box and fields
        phosphor: #6dff8a, main text, prompts, glow, the inverse bar and focus
        dim: #4cd468, secondary text, line numbers, removed lines and box titles
        trace: #2a7a3c, box rules and the dashed separators, never text
        inverseInk: #031a08, text on the phosphor inverse bar and the primary button
    type:
        One monospace stack, IBM Plex Mono, DejaVu Sans Mono, Liberation Mono,
        ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, at 15px on 1.6 for everything. The title is
        20px at 700 in caps. Prompts are 15px at 700. Box titles 13px in dim. Every
        glyph glows with a 4px phosphor text shadow.
    layout:
        A single left aligned transcript column, max 1000px, on flat black with a
        faint radial vignette. A full width inverse status line reads Brightwork
        Code, the repository and Private. Then a series of prompts, each followed by
        its output. bw repo view prints Watch 12, Star 48 and Fork 3 and a numbered
        tab menu where Pull requests sits in inverse video. bw pr view 214 prints a
        ruled box with the title, the Open state, the merge sentence and a two
        column key and value list for reviewers, labels, assignees, milestone and
        linked issue. bw pr checks prints all twelve checks as aligned rows with a
        mark and a word and a twelve cell text meter. bw pr diff prints the three
        file totals and the hunk with plus and minus signs and Tomás Ruiz's comment
        boxed inline. bw pr merge prints the block reason and a bracketed disabled
        Merge button. A block cursor blinks on the last prompt. At 375px the same
        column narrows and wide output scrolls inside its own box.
    spacing: A line based rhythm of 24px. One blank line between commands, 16px box padding.
    density: Medium. Text only, aligned in columns, no cards.
    corners: Square everywhere.
    borders:
        1px trace rules around output boxes, dashed trace separators between
        commands, inverse video for the status line and the current tab.
    shadows: No box shadows. Text has a 4px phosphor glow at 55 percent.
    icons:
        Line icons at 2px stroke drawn in phosphor at 1em with square caps, plus the
        word. Check circle for passed and approved, crossed square for failing,
        triangle with a bang for requested changes, padlock for the blocked merge,
        the pull request glyph for Open.
    focus: Inverse video, a phosphor fill with inverseInk text, plus a 2px phosphor outline offset 2px.
    tone: Machine terse in prompts and output, such as 11/12 passed and merge blocked, 1 check failing.
